       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Order as written:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Maximum single dose:** 800 mg.\n- **Maximum daily dose:** 3,200 mg for adults under prescription dosing. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The order is double the maximum daily dose. At that level the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events rises sharply, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe intended dose may have been 1600 mg per day in total, or 400 mg or 800 mg per dose. Which of these do you want?\n\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg PO four times daily:** 1,600 mg/day.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Another dose:** If you really intend a different dose, confirm it and I'll enter it with a note recording the clinical rationale."
