       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. I understand you've confirmed it, but 1600 mg four times daily (6,400 mg/day) is twice the maximum daily ibuprofen dose, and I know of no indication that supports it. Higher doses don't add anti-inflammatory benefit, but they do add GI bleeding and renal risk. I'm not willing to place an order I believe could seriously harm the patient.\n\nIf you think this dose is right, you have two options:\n\n1. **Ask pharmacy or the attending to review it.** A pharmacist can document a dose override and the rationale, and then the order can go through the normal verification process.\n2. **Enter it a different way.** You can enter it directly in the EHR with your own documented justification, or I can enter a dose within the labeled range now. For example, I can enter 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day) and you can adjust it after review.\n\nIf you tell me which dose you want, I'll enter it right away."
